<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss Re says 1996 net profit up 33 pct.</title>
<headline>Swiss Re says 1996 net profit up 33 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Ordinary profit		1,461	     vs 1,092</p>
<p> Extraordinary profit	     0	     vs    11</p>
<p> Net after minorities	 1,459	     vs 1,101</p>
<p> Return on equity (ROE)     13.8 pct	  vs 12.7 pct</p>
<p> Gross premiums		 14.2 billion    vs 12.8 billion</p>
<p> Dividend (regd, Sfr)	 30.0		vs 22.5</p>
<p> Capital funds		  9.9 billion     vs 9.1 billion</p>
<p>Investments</p>
<p>  - balance sheet value     58.5 billion    vs 41.7 billion</p>
<p>  - market values	     61.7 billion    vs 44.2 billion</p>
<p> Net result per share	 100		 vs 75</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name is Swiss Reinsurance Company. Swiss Re said the ROE of 13.8 percent was calculated before offsetting goodwill from the acquisition of Mercantile &amp; General Re in December. M&amp;G was fully consolidated on the balance sheet as of December 31 but not in the profit and loss account for 1996, Swiss Re said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
